arget.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3853,"endPos":3918,"startLine":89,"startLineOffset":14,"endLine":89,"endLineOffset":79,"length":66}]}]},{"comment":"`Releasables.wrap()` with zero varargs produces a `Releasable` whose `close()` is a no-op. Using it as a `static final` singleton placeholder is appropriate and avoids repeated allocation.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/recovery/RecoveryTarget.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/recovery/RecoveryTarget.java--4115:4221","promptId":"#9D3XQ","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/recovery/RecoveryTarget.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/recovery/RecoveryTarget.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":4115,"endPos":4221,"startLine":93,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":93,"endLineOffset":110,"length":107}]}]},{"comment":"A clarifying comment for the new placeholder field. Clear and helpful.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/recovery/RecoveryTarget.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/recovery/RecoveryTarget.java--3985:4110","promptId":"#5R149","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/recovery/RecoveryTarget.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/indices/recovery/RecoveryTarget.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3985,"endPos":4110,"startLine":92,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":92,"endLineOffset":129,"length":126}]}]},{"comment":"Replacing `null` with the no-op placeholder prevents potential `NullPointerException` or failed null-checks in code paths that dereference `snapshotFileDownloadsPermit` on a replaced (but not yet fully released) `RecoveryTarget`. The behavioral change is that `snapshotFileDownloadsPermit !\u003d null` is now `true` during retry instead of `false`; any code using a null-check to gate snapshot-file-download logic will now take the \"permit present\" branch, but since the permit\u0027s `close()` is a no-op, the